Stage 1 Trivy operator

You will add the platform-trivy namespace

Create a new directory inside infra/Kubernetes/k3-d/helm-charts called trivy. Do all your working in this directory for this stage
Add a simple chart for trivy operator oci://ghcr.io/aquasecurity/helm-charts/trivy-operator

helm repo add aqua https://aquasecurity.github.io/helm-charts/
helm repo update

helm upgrade --install trivy-operator aqua/trivy-operator \
  --namespace platform-trivy \
  --create-namespace \
  --version 0.38.0


Verify that scanning works
kubectl get pods -n platform-trivy
kubectl logs -n platform-trivy deployment/trivy-operator

Then inspect reports across your cluster (if nothing is deployed deploy something simple to check)
kubectl get vulnerabilityreports -A
kubectl get configauditreports -A
kubectl get rbacassessmentreports -A

Stage 2 Trivy UI:

You will add the platform-trivy-ui namespace.

If you need to look at docs: https://github.com/locustbaby/trivy-ui

create a new directory inside infra/Kubernetes/k3-d/helm-charts called trivy-ui. Do all your working in this directory for this stage
Add a simple chart for trivy ui
oci://registry-1.docker.io/locustbaby/trivy-ui

create a simple bcrypt hash 

Create auth.yaml with this
version: v1
users:
  admin:
    passwordHash: "$YOUR_GENERATED_BCRYPT_HASH"
    scopes:
      - cluster: "*"
        namespaces: ["*", "_"]



kubectl create secret generic trivy-ui-auth \
  -n platform-trivy \
  --from-file=auth.yaml=auth.yaml \
  --from-literal=session-secret="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"

Add a simple values file with auth mode: local and auth.local.existingSecret download and check the chart with helm show values to make sure you get syntax right.

Expose it through Traefik
 you can use the same IngressRoute pattern as your Grafana and Nextcloud routes. First, confirm the actual Service name and port created by the chart:
kubectl get svc -n platform-trivy Assuming the Service is named trivy-ui and exposes port 80, the route would look like this:


Add the following inside infra/Kubernetes/k3d-dev/templates/traefik/sample-ingressroute.yaml seperated by '---' like the other routes.
# Trivy UI — public HTTPS route
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: trivy-ui-secure
  namespace: platform-trivy
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - websecure
  routes:
    - match: Host(`trivy-ui-demo.duckdns.org`)
      kind: Rule
      services:
        - name: trivy-ui
          port: 80
  tls:
    secretName: trivy-ui-tls

The Service name and port should match the output of kubectl get svc.

Do not apply the ingress it will be used later on.

verify everything:
kubectl get pods,svc -n platform-trivy
kubectl logs -n platform-trivy deployment/trivy-ui
kubectl get vulnerabilityreports -A

